<!--
  Reconstructed. Assembled from the published API reference, Forums "Threading", with
  no literal XML sample for a reply entry:

    "The replies feed is FLAT... From Standalone_forum_reply_entry_
    content_70, the three attributes on <thr:in-reply-to> do distinct
    jobs: ref = LSID of the immediate parent (a topic or another
    reply); href = fetchable URL of that immediate parent; source =
    top level parent topic of this reply." Type marker
    forum-reply via scheme=".../sn/type"; flags scheme=".../sn/flags"
    documents "answer" applying to replies.

  Encodes the flat-feed reply -> reply -> topic chain the Testing section calls for: reply-1 replies directly to the topic
  (ref = topic uuid); reply-2 replies to reply-1 (ref = reply-1's own
  uuid, NOT the topic) — depth 2 reconstructable only via
  build_reply_tree, since this feed carries no nesting of its own.
  reply-3 is a second, independent top-level reply, marked "answer",
  to prove multiple flat roots and a flag both come through correctly.
  All three share source = the topic uuid (88888888-...) from
  forums_topics_feed.xml's first entry.
-->
